A rainbow poem can't be black and white
Like old cinema
Or as the hipster photographs adorning the walls of a flat in Hackney,
A rainbow poem yells for the joy of its colours!!!
The rainbow poem has the cheerful energy of the yellow
The boldness of the orange
The quirkiness of the purple
The confort of a blue sky 
mirrowing the sea...
The beauty of a green meadow 
in a sunny winter day
The driving force of the red,
As the blood in our veins and the magma inside the earth.
If you mix and match the colours of the rainbow
you get the colours of life


